From 631247529db4d76c0314c70d848b5fb66e98d242 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 13:36:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Phase 4+5: language branch (CLIP + CoOp context tokens)
 and real TG-FEM math

Phase 4 (src/tgfem/language.py):
- TextEncoder: frozen CLIP ViT-B/32 text tower via open_clip. Falls back to a
  randomly-initialised encoder of the same architecture with a loud warning
  when huggingface.co is unreachable (this sandbox has no route to it) -
  keeps the pipeline mechanically testable everywhere while making clear
  embeddings carry no semantic meaning until pretrained_loaded is True.
- ContextTokenLearner: CoOp-style learnable context tokens, spliced into
  CLIP's frozen embedding space and run through the frozen transformer fresh
  on every call so gradients reach the context vectors (M=0 reproduces
  hand-written prompts for ablation (d)).
- TextConditioner: owns the language branch, registers a forward_pre_hook
  on the root model that recomputes T and populates every TGFEM.txt (and
  txt_feats for WorldDetect) before each forward pass. Implemented as a
  bound-method callable (not a closure) so it survives Ultralytics'
  pickle-based checkpointing.

Phase 5 (src/tgfem/module.py):
- Real TG-FEM math: 1x1 projection -> region-text attention -> dual
  channel/spatial gating from the text-conditioned response S -> residual.
  Fixes the report's F'=F(*)g(*)s+F identity bug: gates are zero-init so the
  module starts near-identity as gates->0, not gates->1.
- proj/channel_gate are materialised lazily from the actual input channel
  count (parse_model never passes c1 to unrecognised modules - Phase 2
  finding) so identity and active modes carry the same parameter budget,
  which is what makes ablation (a) valid.
- src/tgfem/detection_model.py (TGFEMModel) + src/tgfem/trainer.py
  (TGFEMTrainer): swap the head to Ultralytics' own WorldDetect +
  ContrastiveHead (region-text contrastive classification, README
  component table row 5) and thread text into it the same way WorldModel
  does, since TG-FEM's attention alone doesn't make the model open-vocab -
  the classification branch has to compare region embeddings against text
  too. ctx is exposed as model.tgfem_ctx (same Parameter object, weight-tied)
  so Trainer.build_optimizer picks it up automatically.
- cfg/yolo11-tgfem.yaml, cfg/yolo11-tgfem-ablation-a.yaml (ablation (a),
  same param budget, identity=True), cfg/yolo11-cbam-worlddetect.yaml
  (ablation (g): CBAM gates + WorldDetect head, isolating gate source from
  classification head - distinct from the existing yolo11-cbam.yaml, which
  stays as the Phase 3 closed-vocab retention baseline).
- scripts/train_tgfem_gate.py: Phase 2-style walking-skeleton gate check,
  now covering the real math - structure, WorldDetect presence, gradient
  reaching context tokens (verified they actually move after training),
  TGFEM materialising real parameters, checkpoint round-trip, and boxes
  coming out the far end. Passes end to end on CPU.

Sandbox constraints (documented in language.py and the gate script): no
GPU and no route to huggingface.co here, so this validates wiring, not
accuracy - re-run with real CLIP weights and GPU access before trusting any
number.
